From: Learning (F, claude/r7-learning)
Subject: [PATCH 021] her joints authored per topic: the script's `joints` block (D13, dc-r7-script-walk-v6-10)

The four sentences code says word for word in every lesson are why register sits at 3 (director18): the aside park ("Cricket ki
baat hum thodi der mein karenge."), the aside return ("Ab tumhari cricket wali baat: usmein tumhe sabse achha kya lagta hai?"),
the language switch ("Theek hai, ab Hindi mein.") and the ask-again line. From D13 each lesson script carries them, per topic.

CONTRACT (data; validated by scripts/lesson-scripts/check.mjs `jointErrors`, on every v2.3 script):

  "joints": {
    "asidePark":   [{ hi, en } × ≥3],   // may use {aside}; promises no "question" (none may be open); asks nothing
    "asideReturn": [{ hi, en } × ≥3],   // every form has {said}; may use {aside}; picks up what the child said ("sixer")
    "hindiSwitch": [{ hi, en } × ≥3],   // hi is said on a switch to Hindi, en on a switch to English; asks nothing
    "askAgain":    [{ hi, en } × ≥3]    // the ask-again line when her ear could not make out the words
  }

  - three distinct forms per kind (a single authored sentence is said every time: the inherited law), each ≤ 16 words;
  - slots: {aside} = the topic the child raised (ret.topic); {said} = their own words, cut to ≤ 6 (ret.said); no other slot;
  - no form names a topic the child did not raise (no "cricket" in data);
  - the format stays 2.3 (no SCRIPT_VERSIONS change): `joints` is a new top-level key of a 2.3 script, and Brain's validator
    already ignores it. The four pilots carry it now (claude/r7-learning); the regenerated staged batch carries it too.

BRAIN'S HALF (the diff below is server/brain/say.js only; it is a proposal against int/r6 851b1bb8f — `git apply --check` clean):

1. say.js: `jointForms(state, kind, lang)` turns the authored forms into the same (topic, said) => line functions freshForm
   already rotates, so a form is never said within 4 turns of itself. Code's sets (RETURN_Q, PARK_ACK / PARK_LATER, LANG_ACK)
   stay as the fallback for a topic without a script.
2. returnQuestion(topic, lang, state, said): the return uses asideReturn with {said} = ret.said (both call sites pass said0).
3. parkAckOf: asidePark when present (an authored park promises no question, so it fits an open card and no card alike).
4. langAckOf(state, lang): hindiSwitch.hi / .en when present, at both LANG_ACK sites.

Not in the diff, and Brain's to wire:
- put the script's joints on the lesson context where the walk loads the script (e.g. `s.ctx.joints = scriptFor(kit)?.script?.joints
  ?? null` at lesson start / topic switch), so say.js reads `state.ctx.joints`;
- askAgain: state.js silentTurn's unheard path plans SH.unheardAgain() (a model shape). With joints present, render one authored
  askAgain form (freshForm over jointForms(state, "askAgain", lang)) as the move's `rendered` line instead of asking the model.
- tests: one per kind — a script with joints says an authored form (and {said} carries "sixer maara" into the return); a topic
  without a script keeps code's set; no form repeats within 4 turns.

